  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members) completed per RBC-QM-02.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Open gap – FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003), outreach message sent (comm-t0005) | No qualifying screening on record. The frailty + advanced illness exclusion does not apply: Dr. Lin's message of 10/23 marked the Frailty entry (cond-00189) as entered in error. Without frailty, the donepezil order alone does not exclude her. No hospice/palliative care; lives at home. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice episode eoc-00002 was active 06/16–08/21/2026 and is now finished. A finished episode still counts. The hospice discharge summary that arrived today (revoked to enter a clinical trial) confirms this. No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (52) | Open gap – FIT kit ordered (sr-t0004), outreach message sent (comm-t0006) | The lab corrected the negative FIT obs-01732 today: it was collected 12/31/2025, and 01/05/2026 was the lab receipt date. That puts it outside the measurement period. No other qualifying test; past oral cancers are not CRC. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap – FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001), outreach message sent (comm-t0002) | The 06/2024 sDNA-FIT (obs-01871) is entered in error: Harbor Lab says the specimen belonged to another patient (doc-00401). The 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 was never done, and an order does not count. No exclusion. |\n\nAll FIT windows run 10/23–12/31/2026, and none of these patients had an active FIT order before. I wrote a protocol note in each chart (doc-t0007 to t0010). I reviewed and completed the 4 inbox items that arrived at the start of the work (inbox-a0001 to a0004); each one was taken into account before any decision was recorded, so nothing needed reversing. No new arrivals came in after that.\n\nFor Dr. Okafor: pt-0024's 2025 colonoscopy order is still active and was never completed, and she has not been told the lab withdrew her 2024 result. I left the unrelated inbox items as they were.",
